@participant2 The log file indicates that none of the fonts discovered by wezterm include that codepoint.
Part of the fallback processing involves asking the DirectWrite layer to suggest fonts with matching codepoints, and it appears that none were suggested by DirectWrite.

What font actually contains that codepoint on your system?

> @participant2 yes, i've used the nerdfix to get all the missing symbols in the nerd fonts.

@participant4 - as far as I can tell, `nerdfix` will identify and replace missing symbols from a project.  That could be a directory or a file.  How do I apply this tool in this instance? What should my target be? I'm not sure where the symbol originates from.

Thanks in advance.

@participant2 
1. Copy in paste the symbol in to a file, use ```nerdfix fix filename```
2. Get or generate a list of the most popular symbols use nerdfix to get all the missing symbols. (option I've used)
